  "raw": {
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4337861": {
      "title": "Westminster College - Instructor of Health and Exercise Science",
      "description": "Westminster College - Instructor of Health and Exercise Science In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Instructor of Health and Exercise Science Westminster College Apply Instructor of Health and Exercise Science Fulton, MO • Health and Exercise Science Apply Job Type Part-time Description At Westminster College, we believe in immersive and enriching experiences that inspire creative thinking and problem solving. We believe in creating opportunities for several different paths to success over a lifetime and the potential to make an impact from wherever you are. For our students, we do this by providing real-world, hands-on learning opportunities, small class sizes, and talented professors dedicated to the individual. Our employees often remark that our tight-knit community creates an atmosphere fostering campus involvement that adapts to all interests. As a result, Westminster continues to be recognized for its excellence in higher education as one of the best small liberal arts colleges in the Midwest. The Health and Exercise Science department at Westminster College seeks a well-qualified part-time instructor for teaching undergraduate courses for the Fall 2026 semester. The successful candidate may teach one or more of the following: Care and Prevention of Athletic Injuries (3-credit hours); First Aid and CPR (1-credit hour). Additional courses may be available for the Spring semester. All regular semester courses are taught in-person on campus. The Health and Exercise Science department also provides training and mentoring for our instructors. Instructors are part-time, non-benefit eligible, teaching positions filled semester-by-semester as needed. Requirements Job Requirements: Education: At minimum an earned Master's degree in Exercise Science, Athletic Training, Kinesiology, or related-field. Experience: The ideal candidate has teaching experience in higher education and takes a personal interest in student success. Compensation: Compensation for teaching a course is $1,000/ credit-hour. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS : 1) Cover letter 2) Current curriculum vitae 3) Unofficial graduate transcripts 4) At least two academic or professional references Official transcripts must be submitted prior to the first day of official employment for the selected applicant. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled or the search is closed. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4436602": {
      "title": "Westminster College - Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Westminster College - Maintenance Technician In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Maintenance Technician Westminster College Apply Maintenance Technician Fulton, MO • Plant Operations; Maintenance Apply Job Type Full-time Description At Westminster College, we believe in immersive and enriching experiences that inspire creative thinking and problem solving. We believe in creating opportunities for several different paths to success over a lifetime and the potential to make an impact from wherever you are. For our students, we do this by providing real-world, hands-on learning opportunities, small class sizes, and talented professors dedicated to the individual. Our employees often remark that our tight-knit community creates an atmosphere fostering campus involvement that adapts to all interests. As a result, Westminster continues to be recognized for its excellence in higher education as one of the best small liberal arts colleges in the Midwest. The Maintenance Technician role provides skilled and semi-skilled repairs and preventive maintenance services to campus facilities. Requirements Essential Functions: Performing a variety of tasks relating to electrical work – troubleshooting, re-lamping, repairing or replacing fixtures, switches, outlets, ballasts, and covers. Performing a variety of tasks relating to carpentry work – installing shelves, bulletin boards, dispensers, pictures; repairing/replacing/installing building components such as walls, doors, ceilings, floors, hardware, partitions, shelving, bulletin boards, dispensers, minor exterior building repairs. Performing a variety of tasks relating to plumbing work – maintaining and repairing sinks, toilets, faucets, dispensers, fountains and pipes; clear obstructions from water, sewer lines, drains and sump pumps. May perform a variety of tasks relating to Plant Operations work as needed; must maintain a valid Missouri driver’s license. Job Requirements: Education: High school diploma or equivalent. Experience: Five years experience responsible for general facilities maintenance. Skills: Skilled in the application of maintenance, renovation, and repairs following recognized principles and practices of the trades associated with electrical, carpentry, and plumbing. Skilled in safe operation of equipment and tools. Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision options Health Savings Account and/or Flex Spending Account Supplemental options: Short-term disability, Hospitalization, Accident, and Critical Illness Stand-alone EAP program Life, AD&D, and long-term disability Retirement 403(b) plan Tuition remission or exchange programs Sick and Vacation time Paid Holidays (15+ each year) Westminster College encourages and gives full consideration to all applicants for admission, financial aid, and employment. The College is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. The College does not discriminate in access to, treatment of, or employment in, its programs and activities on the basis of race, color, age, religion, sex, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national or ethnic origin, citizenship, veteran status, marital status, disability, or genetic information. Inquiries about compliance with this prohibition should be directed to: Associate Vice President & Chief HR Officer/Title IX Coordinator 501 Westminster Ave, Washington West, 2nd floor Fulton, MO 65251 HR@Westminster-mo.edu 573-592-5226 Salary Description Non-Exempt Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
