    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3792340": {
      "title": "Westminster College - Director of Annual Giving",
      "description": "Westminster College - Director of Annual Giving In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Director of Annual Giving Westminster College Apply Director of Annual Giving Fulton, MO • Institutional Advancement Apply Job Type Full-time Description Under the supervision of the Vice President for Institutional Advancement and Alumni Relations, the Director works with donors to maximize annual, unrestricted support for Westminster College.  The primary role of this position is to oversee and direct the Westminster Fund program, working to meet an annual fundraising goal through direct mail, email, volunteer solicitations, phone-a-thons, and significant donor programs (Presidents Club, True Blue).  Annual Giving should be designed to capitalize on existing engagement programs in the alumni and marketing offices and to feed prospects to the major gifts program.  This position is an on campus position. Requirements Essential Functions: The statements below are intended to describe the principal duties of the person or persons assigned to this job. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all job duties and responsibilities. Planning and implementing a comprehensive annual fund program, including mail, phone, and electronic solicitations that are appropriately segmented, timed, and coordinated with other offices. Recruiting and coordinating volunteers for the President’s Club, True Blue, and other annual giving societies. Identifying, cultivating, and soliciting annual major donors ($5,000 and above) to the Westminster Fund. Analyzing annual fund donors to identify major gift and planned gift prospects. Overseeing a comprehensive stewardship program for donors to the Westminster Fund, engaging staff, faculty, trustees, and volunteers as necessary. Recruiting, hiring, training, and supervising student callers. Representing the college during events and gatherings, as assigned by the VPIA. Serving as Westminster’s primary liaison to the Fulton Colleges Fund and Board of Associates and supporting their local fundraising efforts. The ability to work independently and strategically to achieve fundraising goals. Limited travel to facilitate solicitations of select major annual fund prospects. JOB REQUIREMENTS: Education: Bachelor 's degree from an accredited institution, Master's degree preferred. Experience: At least two years of experience working in institutional advancement or other fundraising efforts, including an ability to understand and apply best practices.  Experience with data management. Experience working with diverse populations.  Experience contributing to campus diversity efforts. Skills: Strong writing and communications skills Ability to multi-task and be detail and deadline oriented Experience working with volunteers An understanding of liberal arts education and its place in the broader world of higher education A willingness to work on a team to establish goals, strategies, and implementation of programs Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled or the search is closed. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4472560": {
      "title": "Westminster College - Assistant Registrar",
      "description": "Westminster College - Assistant Registrar In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Assistant Registrar Westminster College Apply Assistant Registrar Fulton, MO • Academic Affairs - Registrar's Office Apply Job Type Full-time Description At Westminster College, we believe in immersive and enriching experiences that inspire creative thinking and problem solving. We believe in creating opportunities for several different paths to success over a lifetime and the potential to make an impact from wherever you are. For our students, we do this by providing real-world, hands-on learning opportunities, small class sizes, and talented professors dedicated to the individual. Our employees often remark that our tight-knit community creates an atmosphere fostering campus involvement that adapts to all interests. As a result, Westminster continues to be recognized for its excellence in higher education as one of the best small liberal arts colleges in the Midwest. Reporting to the Registrar, the Assistant Registrar supports the administration of student records, registration services, transfer credit evaluation, degree audit processes, and student information system operations. This position serves as a primary resource for students, faculty, and staff regarding academic policies, transfer credit, registration, and student record maintenance. The Assistant Registrar is responsible for ensuring the integrity, accuracy, confidentiality, and security of student educational records in compliance with applicable state, federal, and accreditation regulations, including FERPA, as well as college policies and procedures. This position frequently exercises independent judgement in resolving student record issues, maintaining course equivalencies, evaluating transfer credit, and supporting the daily operations of the Registrar Office while providing responsive and student-centered service. Requirements Essential Functions: The statements below are intended to describe the principal duties of the person or persons assigned to this job. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all job duties and responsibilities. Maintain accurate, organized, and confidential student academic records within the student information system; process student record forms; perform data entry, validation, and quality-control activities; and ensure compliance with established records-retention policies and procedures. Process student registration and academic record transactions, including course additions, drops, withdrawals, course waitlists, schedule adjustments, and other approved record changes. Coordinate and maintain student applications and related records for consortia, MMACU, and other approved program enrollments. Manage classroom calendars through Outlook and Jenzabar. Assist with office walk-in and telephone inquiries, monitor and respond to Registrar’s Office emails. Assist with student communications related to registration, graduation, academic standing, and other Registrar's Office processes. Comply with the College procedures, guidelines, and regulations relating to FERPA and confidentiality of information. Process requests for academic transcripts and degree verifications through the National Student Clearinghouse and provide legacy transcripts as needed. Evaluate and process transfer credit and other external sources of academic credit, including examination-based credit (e.g., AP, CLEP, IB), dual-credit coursework, international credentials (e.g., A-Levels, Abitur, and other international secondary or postsecondary credentials), and transfer coursework from accredited institutions in accordance with established transfer credit policies and procedures. Verify, document, and maintain records of the accreditation status of institutions from which transfer or other external academic credit is accepted in accordance with institutional policies and procedures. Collaborate with academic departments to evaluate transfer coursework and establish course equivalencies in the Transfer Evaluation System (TES). Maintain the Transfer Evaluation System (TES) and update course equivalencies as needed. Support the implementation of transfer guides, articulation agreements, and memoranda of understanding by maintaining accurate transfer information and related records within institutional systems. Prepare routine reports and data extracts related to transfer credit, registration, enrollment, graduation, and student records as requested. Serve as a backup for essential Registrar functions and help ensure continuity of operations during staff absences. Work closely with members of the Office of Academic Affairs and provide assistance when needed. Assists with the commencement ceremony and other internal events as needed. Support the Registrar with additional tasks as needed. Other duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Skills: Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills Sincere dedication to exceptional customer service Ability to produce high quality, accurate work in a fast-paced environment Ability to multitask and provide attention to detail Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision options Health Savings Account and/or Flex Spending Account Supplemental options: Short-term disability, Hospitalization, Accident, and Critical Illness Stand-alone EAP program Life, AD&D, and long-term disability Retirement 403(b) plan Tuition remission or exchange programs Sick and Vacation time Paid Holidays (15+ each year) Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled or the search is closed. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3584583": {
      "title": "Westminster College",
      "description": "Westminster College - Custodian - Shift 2 In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Custodian - Shift 2 Westminster College Apply Custodian - Shift 2 Fulton, MO • Plant Operations Apply Job Type Full-time Description At Westminster College, we believe in immersive and enriching experiences that inspire creative thinking and problem solving. We believe in creating opportunities for several different paths to success over a lifetime and the potential to make an impact from wherever you are. For our students, we do this by providing real-world, hands-on learning opportunities, small class sizes, and talented professors dedicated to the individual. Our employees often remark that our tight-knit community creates an atmosphere fostering campus involvement that adapts to all interests. As a result, Westminster continues to be recognized for its excellence in higher education as one of the best small liberal arts colleges in the Midwest. Our Custodians provide a safe, attractive, comfortable, and clean environment to ensure full and productive use of facilities. This is accomplished through performing daily and non-routine cleaning of campus buildings and facilities, moving furniture, and assisting with set ups for events on campus. The primary responsibility is for the effective use of proper methods, use chemicals and materials in maintaining cleanliness, appearance, and sanitation. The full-time Custodian typically works 40 hours a week and must work closely with the supervisor, staff, and administration of the College. This shift is scheduled Monday - Friday from 8:00am to 4:30pm. Requirements Essential Functions: The statements below are intended to describe the principal duties of the person or persons assigned to this job. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all job duties and responsibilities. Dust mops, sweeps, wet mops, spray-buffs, strips and refinishes floors Vacuums, spot cleans, shampoos carpeting Scrubs and cleans restroom fixtures and keeps restrooms supplied with soap and paper supplies Dusts, cleans, washes walls, doors, windows, woodwork and other above floor surfaces Removes trash from receptacles Sets up rooms for conferences, lectures, and special events Moves furniture Notifies immediate supervisor of equipment and facilities needing repair or replacement Performs related work as required and instructed Assists with set up of tables and chairs for events Lock up college facilities Performs deep cleaning activities as necessary May assist with painting during breaks Job Requirements: Education: High School Diploma or equivalent. Must have a valid driver’s license. Skills: Ability to adhere to departmental operating and safety procedures Ability to perform manual tasks requiring moderate physical strength Ability to operate mechanical cleaning equipment Ability to operate campus vehicle Ability to follow simple oral and written instruction in the conduct of the job Ability to establish and maintain working relations with supervisors, fellow workers, and customers Ability work overtime when required Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision options Health Savings Account and/or Flex Spending Account Supplemental options: Short-term disability, Hospitalization, Accident, and Critical Illness Stand-alone EAP program Life, AD&D, and long-term disability Retirement 403(b) plan Tuition remission or exchange programs Sick and Vacation time Paid Holidays (15+ each year) Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled or the search is closed. Salary Description $15.60/Hour Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
