    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4200600": {
      "title": "Westminster College - Director of Corporate Partnership Development",
      "description": "Westminster College - Director of Corporate Partnership Development In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Director of Corporate Partnership Development Westminster College Apply Director of Corporate Partnership Development Fulton, MO • Enrollment Management Apply Description The Director of Corporate Partnership Development and Employer Success Manager will lead the design, growth, and execution of Westminster College’s Corporate Partnerships Program, expanding access to bachelor’s degree completion opportunities, or life long learning education for working adults while strengthening regional workforce development. This role serves as the senior relationship manager for employer partners and is responsible for driving enrollment growth through strategic outreach, partnership development, and employer-based engagement initiatives. The Director will oversee the full partnership lifecycle—from prospecting and securing agreements to onboarding employees and sustaining long-term employer relationships. This position emphasizes deliberate, data-informed growth, strong external partnerships, and a high-touch, service-oriented enrollment experience aligned with Westminster’s academic mission and student success priorities. At Westminster College, we believe in immersive and enriching experiences that inspire creative thinking and problem solving. We believe in creating opportunities for several different paths to success over a lifetime and the potential to make an impact from wherever you are. For our students, we do this by providing real-world, hands-on learning opportunities, small class sizes, and talented professors dedicated to the individual. Our employees often remark that our tight-knit community creates an atmosphere fostering campus involvement that adapts to all interests. As a result, Westminster continues to be recognized for its excellence in higher education as one of the best small liberal arts colleges in the Midwest. Requirements Essential Functions: The statements below are intended to describe the principal duties of the person or persons assigned to this job. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all job duties and responsibilities. Partnership Development & External Relations Identify, cultivate, and secure partnerships with employers across healthcare, education, manufacturing, logistics, and public sector organizations Prospect and negotiate Memoranda of Understanding (MOUs) that define partnership benefits, eligibility, and renewal terms Serve as the primary point of contact for employer partners, maintaining relationships with HR, Talent Acquisition, and Learning & Development leaders Represent Westminster College in regional workforce development initiatives, employer meetings, and community engagements Enrollment Growth & Employer Engagement Lead enrollment generation through employer-based strategies, including on-site Admissions Days, information sessions, and virtual events Develop and execute a targeted outreach strategy within the defined regional market (approximately 90-mile radius) Build and manage a pipeline of employer partners and prospective students, leveraging CRM tools and data analytics Program Implementation & Student Success Collaborate with Admissions, Financial Aid, Advising, Academic Affairs, and Marketing to ensure seamless onboarding and support for corporate partner students Support program delivery aligned with working adult needs, including structured course pacing and early-term success strategies Ensure employer-specific processes (e.g., admission workflows, transcript evaluation, onboarding) are efficient and student-centered Marketing & Communication Oversee development of employer-specific marketing materials, co-branded collateral, and communications campaigns Collaborate with internal marketing teams to promote partnership benefits and drive awareness among employee populations Data, Reporting & Continuous Improvement Track key metrics including partnership growth, inquiries, applications, enrollments, and student persistence Conduct regular partner reviews and use performance data to refine strategy and improve outcomes Contribute to program evaluation, expansion planning, and long-term sustainability efforts Job Requirements: Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution required; master’s degree preferred. Experience: Minimum of five years of experience in workforce partnerships, employer relations, enrollment management, business development, or related field. Skills : · Strong communication, presentation, and relationship-building skills · Proven ability to manage multiple projects and partnerships simultaneously · Experience using CRM systems and data to drive strategy and decision-making · Ability to work both independently and collaboratively across departments · High level of organization, initiative, and attention to detail · Ability to build trust with external stakeholders and internal partners Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision options Health Savings Account and/or Flex Spending Account Supplemental options: Short-term disability, Hospitalization, Accident, and Critical Illness Stand-alone EAP program Life, AD&D, and long-term disability Retirement 403(b) plan Tuition remission or exchange programs Sick and Vacation time Paid Holidays (15+ each year) Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled or the search is closed. Westminster College encourages and gives full consideration to all applicants for admission, financial aid, and employment. The College does not discriminate in access to, treatment of, or employment in, its programs and activities on the basis of race, color, age, religion, sex, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national or ethnic origin, citizenship, veteran status, marital status, disability, or genetic information. Inquiries about compliance with this prohibition should be directed to: Associate Vice President & Chief HR Officer/Title IX Coordinator 501 Westminster Ave, Washington West, 2nd floor Fulton, MO 65251 HR@Westminster-mo.edu 573-592-5226 Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4496014": {
      "title": "Westminster College - Coordinator of Academic Administrative Services",
      "description": "Westminster College - Coordinator of Academic Administrative Services In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Coordinator of Academic Administrative Services Westminster College Apply Coordinator of Academic Administrative Services Fulton, MO • Academic Affairs Apply Job Type Full-time Description At Westminster College, we believe in immersive and enriching experiences that inspire creative thinking and problem solving. We believe in creating opportunities for several different paths to success over a lifetime and the potential to make an impact from wherever you are. For our students, we do this by providing real-world, hands-on learning opportunities, small class sizes, and talented professors dedicated to the individual. Our employees often remark that our tight-knit community creates an atmosphere fostering campus involvement that adapts to all interests. As a result, Westminster continues to be recognized for its excellence in higher education as one of the best small liberal arts colleges in the Midwest. The Coordinator of Academic Administrative Services provides administrative, operational, financial, and organizational support for the Office of Academic Affairs, including the Registrar and other offices under the supervision of the Provost. The position supports multiple Academic Affairs administrators and manages purchasing, departmental purchase card processes, and budget tracking, while coordinating faculty compensation-related documentation, reimbursements, administrative workflows, and related office operations. The individual in this role must demonstrate professionalism, flexibility, initiative, discretion, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced and collaborative environment. Requirements ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : The statements below are intended to describe the principal duties of the person assigned to this job. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all job duties and responsibilities. Provide administrative and operational support for the Office of Academic Affairs, the Registrar, and Student Success and Retention. Support Academic Affairs administrators, including the Provost, deans, directors, designated committee chairs, and other Academic Affairs personnel as assigned. Provide excellent customer service to faculty, students, staff, and visitors. Coordinate day-to-day office workflows and administrative processes within Academic Affairs. Manage purchasing and departmental purchase card processes, including reconciliation of monthly statements and collection of supporting documentation. Assist faculty and Academic Affairs personnel with travel requests, approvals, reimbursements, and related documentation. Coordinate the preparation, tracking, and processing of faculty compensation-related documentation, including overload assignments, independent studies, stipends, adjunct assignments, and other compensated academic activities. Maintain records and tracking systems related to faculty assignments, compensation processes, reimbursements, purchasing activities, budgets, and other office operations. Coordinate with the Business Office, Human Resources, department chairs, and other institutional offices to support timely processing of documentation and administrative transactions. Coordinate budget tracking and reporting and maintain financial records and documentation for areas under the supervision of the Provost. Create, organize, and maintain shared electronic files, records, office procedures, and administrative documentation systems. Assist with preparation, editing, proofreading, formatting, organization, and distribution of reports, spreadsheets, forms, and related operational materials. Assist with routing, tracking, and processing Academic Affairs administrative forms and related documentation. This includes student and faculty e-forms, evaluations tasks for the Transfer Equivalency System, syllabi and diploma requests. Occasionally assist with data entry and administrative processing within institutional systems, including Jenzabar, as appropriate. Maintain inventory of office and instructional supplies and coordinate ordering as needed. Conduct research, data gathering, reporting support, and special projects as assigned. Schedule meetings, appointments, and other administrative activities as needed. Perform routine office duties such as copying, scanning, filing, and shredding. Work collaboratively with members of the Office of Academic Affairs to support continuity of operations during periods of high workload, staff transitions, or institutional need. Assist with events, such as faculty orientation, Commencement, New Student Convocation, Hancock Symposium etc. Other duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Education: Bachelor’s degree preferred. Experience : Minimum of two years of administrative or operational support experience preferred, in higher education or similar professional office environment. Skills : Strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills; strong organizational abilities; attention to detail; professionalism; discretion and confidentiality; ability to manage multiple responsibilities and deadlines; ability to work independently and collaboratively; and commitment to responsive customer service. The position requires proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook, and other standard office software applications, along with the ability and willingness to learn institutional administrative systems and software platforms. The individual in this position must be able to operate a personal computer and standard office equipment, including telephone, copier, scanner, and related office technology. The physical demands of this position include sitting, standing, reaching, bending, and occasional light lifting in a standard office environment. Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision options Health Savings Account and/or Flex Spending Account Supplemental options: Short-term disability, Hospitalization, Accident, and Critical Illness Stand-alone EAP program Life, AD&D, and long-term disability Retirement 403(b) plan Tuition remission or exchange programs Sick and Vacation time Paid Holidays (15+ each year) Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4488537": {
      "title": "Westminster College - Administrative Coordinator for Student Success and Accessibility",
      "description": "Westminster College - Administrative Coordinator for Student Success and Accessibility In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Administrative Coordinator for Student Success and Accessibility Westminster College Apply Administrative Coordinator for Student Success and Accessibility Fulton, MO • Learning Opportunities Center Apply Job Type Full-time Description At Westminster College, we believe in immersive and enriching experiences that inspire creative thinking and problem solving. We believe in creating opportunities for several different paths to success over a lifetime and the potential to make an impact from wherever you are. For our students, we do this by providing real-world, hands-on learning opportunities, small class sizes, and talented professors dedicated to the individual. Our employees often remark that our tight-knit community creates an atmosphere fostering campus involvement that adapts to all interests. As a result, Westminster continues to be recognized for its excellence in higher education as one of the best small liberal arts colleges in the Midwest. The Administrative Coordinator for Student Success and Accessibility provides administrative, operational, and student success technology support for the Tomnitz Family Learning Opportunities Center (LOC), the First-Year Experience (FYE), and the Student Success Center (SSC). The position serves as the primary administrative resource for accessibility services, specialized academic support programs, and the daily operation of student success initiatives. The position coordinates administrative processes associated with disability accommodations, the Learning Difference Program (LDP), the College Transition Program (CTP), and First-Year Experience activities. The position also provides operational administration for EAB Navigate 360 and supports the effective use of Jenzabar, Slate, and other institutional systems used by Academic Affairs and Student Success. Responsibilities include user administration, documentation, workflow coordination, communication support, record management, routine system maintenance, and coordination with campus partners. Through effective organization, communication, accuracy, and attention to detail, the position facilitates student access to services and supports the College's mission, educational goals, and student persistence and retention efforts. Requirements ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : The statements below are intended to describe the principal duties of the person assigned to this job. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all job duties and responsibilities. 1. Administrative Support and Office Operations Provide administrative and operational support for the Learning Opportunities Center, First-Year Experience, and Student Success Center. Manage calendars, communications, records, reporting, office workflows, and customer service for students, faculty, staff, families, and visitors. Coordinate meetings, correspondence, supplies, and routine office functions. 2. Accessibility Services Coordination Coordinate approved disability accommodations, including testing accommodations, note-taking services, and accessible instructional materials. Maintain confidential accommodation records and documentation in compliance with ADA, FERPA, and institutional policies. Communicate with students and faculty regarding accommodation processes and related services. 3. Academic Support Program Administration Support the administration of the Learning Difference Program and College Transition Program. Maintain participant records, coordinate communications, schedule appointments, and assist students and families throughout program processes. 4. First-Year Experience Support Provide administrative support for orientation, new student programs, course placement processes, advisor assignments, and First-Year Experience initiatives. Assist with communications, scheduling, logistics, and record maintenance for student transition programs. 5. Student Success Technology Support Serve as the operational administrator for EAB Navigate 360 and provide support for Jenzabar, Slate, and other student success systems. Manage user access, maintain documentation, support communication campaigns, assist with reporting, and coordinate issue resolution with campus partners. 6. Records Management and Student Communications Maintain confidential student records and departmental files in compliance with institutional and legal requirements. Support communications, reporting, data quality efforts, placement testing, and other student success initiatives. Proctor ACCUPLACER and other approved placement assessments. Perform other duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Education: Associate degree required; bachelor's degree preferred or high school diploma/GED with significant directly related administrative experience. Experience : Minimum: 3 years of progressively responsible administrative support experience. Experience should include one or more of the following: Higher education administration Student services Disability/accessibility services Academic support programs Database, CRM, or student information systems management Office coordination and records management Skills : Strong interpersonal and communication (oral and written) skills; proficiency in Microsoft Word, Microsoft Exchange, Jenzabar. Proficiency in using general office machines, i.e. multi-line phone, copier, and FAX machine; ability to perform general clerical duties of typing and filing; ability to maintain confidentiality; ability to work as a part of a team; ability to prioritize tasks; and ability to deal with fast-paced office environment. Benefits: Medical, dental, and vision options Health Savings Account and/or Flex Spending Account Supplemental options: Short-term disability, Hospitalization, Accident, and Critical Illness Stand-alone EAP program Life, AD&D, and long-term disability Retirement 403(b) plan Tuition remission or exchange programs Sick and Vacation time Paid Holidays (15+ each year) Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
    }
  },
